cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the tagged release below."
title: "Face-Shape Classification — Preprocessing-Impact Study"
abstract: >-
  Code, fixed data splits, and complete per-run results for an empirical study of how
  data preparation (resize, face crop, in-plane alignment, augmentation) affects
  face-shape classification accuracy across CNN and Vision Transformer architectures.
  Contains the complete results of 56 training runs: a 4-model x 4-preprocessing main
  matrix, two seed replications, and an alignment ablation, together with the fixed data
  split and the scripts for a near-duplicate audit and an identity-level leakage audit of
  that split. The near-duplicate audit has been applied to the committed split; the
  identity audit finds that 16.2% of held-out images share an identity with a training
  image, so the reported absolute accuracies are upper bounds. Audit output files are not
  committed, as regenerating them requires the dataset.
type: software
